From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt <noreply@openwrt.org>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: reinit NPU on DMA init

After a WiFi radio cycle (interface down/up), the WiFi firmware resets
the NPU packet processing state.  Only the DMA ring plumbing is
restored by mt7996_npu_rx_queues_init(), but the offload configuration
(ring PCIe addresses, token sizes, descriptor base addresses) is not
re-sent to the NPU firmware.  This causes the NPU to stop writing
FOE_ID/CRSN into RX DMA descriptors, breaking PPE flow commits for
upload traffic.

Reinitialize the NPU after DMA ring setup, following the same
sequence used in L1 SER recovery: disable IRQs, stop the NPU
firmware, then re-init under mutex.

Skip on first boot when npu_txd_addr has not been allocated yet
(mt7996_npu_hw_init runs after mt7996_dma_init in the probe path).

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <noreply@openwrt.org>
---
--- a/mt7996/dma.c
+++ b/mt7996/dma.c
@@ -948,6 +948,15 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	if (dev->npu_txd_addr[0]) {
+		mt76_npu_disable_irqs(&dev->mt76);
+		mt7996_npu_hw_stop(dev);
+
+		mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+		__mt7996_npu_hw_init(dev);
+		mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
+	}
+
 	netif_napi_add_tx(dev->mt76.tx_napi_dev, &dev->mt76.tx_napi,
 			  mt7996_poll_tx);
 	napi_enable(&dev->mt76.tx_napi);
